      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/bakersfield-ca#faqpage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What certifications and standards does STS support for electronics recycling in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS Electronic Recycling supports compliance with NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 2 guidelines for media sanitization. Under these guidelines, sanitization must render data recovery infeasible through verified methods. Our processes include serial-level chain of custody documentation from pickup in Bakersfield through final material recovery at our Jacksonville and Houston facilities. This documentation supports HIPAA technical safeguards for healthcare providers, SOX requirements for financial institutions, and procurement standards for government agencies throughout Kern County."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas around Bakersfield do you serve for electronics recycling?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We provide electronics recycling services throughout Bakersfield and Kern County including Downtown Bakersfield, Oildale, Rosedale, Greenfield, Southwest Bakersfield, Taft, Delano, and Ridgecrest. Free pickup is available for qualifying volumes from energy sites along SR-58 and I-5, large-scale agricultural operations in the San Joaquin Valley, hospitals, school districts, and municipal facilities."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup free for electronics recycling in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup is free for qualifying volumes from Bakersfield and Kern County organizations. Most energy producers, agribusiness operators, and healthcare systems we serve generate sufficient volume that no transportation fee applies. STS engagements with these sectors typically include scheduled pickups coordinated to minimize operational disruption."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does STS protect data during electronics recycling in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Our documented processes support NIST 800-88 Rev. 2 compliant destruction methods for all media containing sensitive data. According to these guidelines, verification of purge-level sanitization or physical destruction is required. STS provides serial-number-specific certificates of destruction that include destruction method, weight, date, and downstream tracking information. This level of documentation is standard for healthcare providers handling protected health information and for government agencies subject to public records retention rules."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you serve energy and agriculture companies in Kern County?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. California Resources Corporation, Chevron, Grimmway Farms, Bolthouse Fresh Foods, and The Wonderful Company rely on STS for secure, documented electronics recycling for control systems and administrative equipment. STS engagements with these organizations typically include scheduled pickups coordinated around production schedules with full chain of custody and environmental reporting."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What healthcare compliance standards does STS support in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS supports HIPAA technical safeguards for Kern Medical, Adventist Health Bakersfield, and Dignity Health facilities. Healthcare IT managers typically require off-hours coordination, Business Associate Agreements where applicable, and detailed documentation for audit readiness. Our processes meet the requirements of the HIPAA Security Rule for electronic protected health information on disposed devices."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Where is equipment from Bakersfield processed?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Equipment collected in Bakersfield is staged locally and transported to one of our two certified processing facilities in Jacksonville, Texas and Houston, Texas, where all data destruction and material recovery takes place. STS Electronic Recycling, Inc. has served schools, businesses, healthcare systems, and government agencies across all 50 states since 2011."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you offer certificate of destruction for Bakersfield customers?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Every engagement includes serial-number-specific certificates of destruction that document destruction method, weight, date, and downstream tracking. These certificates support compliance audits for healthcare, education, government, and corporate customers throughout Kern County. Certificates are provided after final processing at our certified facilities."
          }
        }
      ]
